{"name":"Mayfly","hex":"#696841","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mayfly","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the many fragile insects of the order Ephemeroptera that develop in fresh water and live very briefly as winged adults.","Characterized by a short duration; short-lived."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mayfly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mayfly","blocks":[{"text":"Mayflies are aquatic insects belonging to the order Ephemeroptera. This order is part of an ancient group of insects termed the Palaeoptera, which also contains dragonflies and damselflies. Over 3,000 species of mayfly are known worldwide, grouped into over 400 genera in 42 families."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Rhithrogena_germanica_subimago_on_Equisetum_hyemale.jpg/330px-Rhithrogena_germanica_subimago_on_Equisetum_hyemale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayfly","wikidata":"Q174273"},{"title":"Mayfly (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Mayfly was an American Christian metal band from Dayton, Ohio, formed in 2011. They have released one extended play, Vereor Deus, Non Dogma, in 2014, with Voluminous Records. On March 14, 2017, the band announced that had disbanded."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayfly_(band)","wikidata":"Q22023185"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Mayfly_nymph_dorsal_view_wing_buds_paired_gills.JPG/500px-Mayfly_nymph_dorsal_view_wing_buds_paired_gills.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Mayfly_nymph_dorsal_view_wing_buds_paired_gills.JPG/500px-Mayfly_nymph_dorsal_view_wing_buds_paired_gills.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMayfly_nymph_dorsal_view_wing_buds_paired_gi